# What never belongs inside the image.
#
# Two principles: (1) your data and your secrets are mounted in at run time, never
# baked into a layer; (2) this machine's run history is not the pipeline.

# Git, and the machine state the pipeline writes as it runs
.git/
.logs/
.postmortem/
.dry-run/
.cache/
.token-calibration.json
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Secrets. The keys reach the container through its environment (env_file in
# docker-compose.yml, or --env-file / -e on docker run), which is also why the app's
# own dotenv load inside the container finds no .env and simply keeps what it was given.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Installed on the host, for the host's platform — the image installs its own
node_modules/

# Your books, and everything the pipeline builds next to them. They are mounted into
# the container at run time; only the folder's README belongs in the image.
epub_source/*
!epub_source/README.md
*.epub

# Per-machine hooks (git-style, gitignored). A hook shells out to whatever the local
# machine has — docker, curl, a private CLI — and none of that exists in this image.
# The README and the samples come along; the real hooks do not.
/hooks/*
!/hooks/README.md
!/hooks/*.sample
